<title>BELGIUM: Bekaert slips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Bekaert slips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian steel cord and wire maker Bekaert SA fell three percent on Thursday as investors took profits, partly on a weaker dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;It's only a small reaction to the recent share price climb,&quot; said trader Damien Crispiels at Bank Degroof.</p>
<p>By 1430 GMT the share was down 3.08 percent at 22,000 francs after a bullish run since early February.</p>
<p>Bekaert is due to publish 1996 results after the 1600 GMT bourse close on March 19.</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
